---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Finch Models and Providers"
  description="Current Finch cloud-provider, subscription, remote-daemon, and experimental local-model support."
  canonicalPath="/models/"
>
  <SiteHeader current="models" />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section id="models">
  <h2 class="sec-title">// SUPPORTED MODELS</h2>

  <h3 class="subsec-title">Local (ONNX Runtime) — profiles exist; routing is experimental</h3>
  <p class="table-note">These families have local profiles and loader support in the source. That is a configuration surface, not a conformance claim: local bootstrap, selection, and provider parity are unfinished, so a configured local profile does not yet guarantee your query ran locally. Artifacts are large and may require Hugging Face access.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="model-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>FAMILY</th>
          <th>SIZES</th>
          <th>FORMAT</th>
          <th>NOTES</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Qwen 2.5</td>
          <td>1.5B · 3B · 7B · 14B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Default local family · size chosen by detected RAM</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Llama 3</td>
          <td>1B · 3B · 8B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Meta · general purpose</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Gemma 2/3</td>
          <td>1B · 2B · 9B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Google · strong reasoning</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Mistral</td>
          <td>7B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Mistral model family · <a href="https://github.com/darwin-finch/finch/blob/main/src/models/ONNX.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">third-party ONNX exports</a> from the <code>microsoft</code> and <code>nvidia</code> organizations on Hugging Face; no <code>onnx-community</code> export</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Phi-3/4</td>
          <td>3.8B · 14B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Microsoft · small + capable</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>DeepSeek Coder</td>
          <td>1.3B · 6.7B</td>
          <td>ONNX</td>
          <td class="bar">Optimised for code generation</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">CoreML execution provider on Apple Silicon · CUDA/ROCm/CPU on Linux via ONNX Runtime · Candle is an alternative backend · see <a href="https://github.com/darwin-finch/finch/blob/main/docs/MODEL_BACKEND_STATUS.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MODEL_BACKEND_STATUS.md</a>, a dated backend investigation rather than routing evidence</p>

  <h3 class="subsec-title">Cloud providers — profiles offered by <code>finch setup</code></h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="model-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>PROVIDER</th>
          <th>AUTHENTICATION</th>
          <th>NOTES</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Claude (Anthropic)</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">Enter an explicit model ID, or refresh the authenticated catalogue</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>OpenAI Platform</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">A model ID your Platform account can reach on Chat Completions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>ChatGPT subscription</td>
          <td>Device login — <code>finch auth login</code></td>
          <td class="bar">Finch-owned transport, pinned to a recorded Codex compatibility commit; drift fails closed. Experimental. Subscription credentials are not API keys and never cross-bind with Platform ones</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Grok (xAI)</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">API billing is separate from Grok/X subscriptions · <a href="https://console.x.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">console.x.ai</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Gemini (Google)</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">AI Studio transport; custom endpoints and paths are rejected</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Mistral</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">European provider with open-weight model families</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Groq</td>
          <td>API key</td>
          <td class="bar">Runs open models on the provider's own hardware</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Ollama · remote Finch daemon</td>
          <td>Profile types in source</td>
          <td class="bar">Configurable; not covered by conformance evidence</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="table-note">Switch between configured profiles with <code>/model &lt;name&gt;</code> (<code>/provider</code> and <code>/teacher</code> remain compatibility aliases) · Conversation history is preserved across a switch · Streaming and tool support vary by provider and model, and cross-provider conformance coverage is still being published · Model availability changes independently of Finch, so pricing and model rankings are deliberately not listed here</p>
</section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
